<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

    <!-- ============================================================================
    Root cause investigation (2026-07-14): the user reported hover/press animations on
    a long list of buttons across every module as either completely absent or passing
    through an unexplained intermediate color, despite each one already having its own
    Background Setters + BrushTransition. Traced against Avalonia's actual Fluent theme
    source (AvaloniaUI/Avalonia @ 12.0.5, src/Avalonia.Themes.Fluent/Controls/Button.xaml):
    the default Button ControlTheme paints :pointerover/:pressed/:disabled Background,
    BorderBrush AND Foreground directly on its own template's ContentPresenter#PART_
    ContentPresenter, with NO Transitions of its own on those properties. That style
    targets a template-internal part directly - not the Button's own Background property
    - so it wins over ANY plain `Setter Property="Background"` on the Button itself,
    unconditionally, the instant a pseudo-class activates, snapping without a transition
    and completely discarding whatever we set at the Button level. This is the exact
    same class of bug already diagnosed once for TextBox's focus ring (CCTextBoxTemplate)
    and for ListBoxItem's selection color (SCSkinListItemTemplate in SkinChangerStyles.
    axaml) - both already fixed by owning the whole template. Every custom Button class
    in this app that wasn't already fully retemplated (CCPaletteRow/UnderscoredButton/
    NavItem were, and were never actually broken) had this same latent bug; it only
    surfaced now because nobody had exercised :pointerover/:pressed by hand before.

    FlatButtonTemplate below is the fix, centralized once instead of copy-pasted per
    button class (the user's own complaint about near-duplicate template blocks scattered
    file-to-file) - a plain Border+ContentPresenter with every color-ish property routed
    through TemplateBinding and BrushTransitions baked in on the properties that actually
    render, so any Style consuming it just needs Background/BorderBrush/Foreground Setters
    per pseudo-class - no per-class Transitions or template boilerplate required anymore.
    Merged into Application.Resources (see App.axaml) alongside NeutralColors.axaml/
    AccentColors.axaml so every module's Styles file can reference it via StaticResource,
    the same way AccentSwitchTemplate already is.
    ============================================================================ -->

    <ControlTemplate x:Key="FlatButtonTemplate" TargetType="Button">
        <Border Name="PART_Border"
                Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}">
            <Border.Transitions>
                <Transitions>
                    <BrushTransition Property="Background" Duration="0:0:0.15"/>
                    <BrushTransition Property="BorderBrush" Duration="0:0:0.15"/>
                </Transitions>
            </Border.Transitions>
            <ContentPresenter Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                               ContentTemplate="{TemplateBinding ContentTemplate}"
                               Foreground="{TemplateBinding Foreground}"
                               Padding="{TemplateBinding Padding}"
                               HorizontalContentAlignment="{TemplateBinding HorizontalContentAlignment}"
                               VerticalContentAlignment="{TemplateBinding VerticalContentAlignment}">
                <ContentPresenter.Transitions>
                    <Transitions>
                        <BrushTransition Property="Foreground" Duration="0:0:0.15"/>
                    </Transitions>
                </ContentPresenter.Transitions>
            </ContentPresenter>
        </Border>
    </ControlTemplate>

</ResourceDictionary>
